    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Hydraulic fracturing technique has been widely used in oil industry. An important topic for hydraulic fracturing is well communication, that is the connection of two wellbores by hydraulic fractures. A boundary element model has been used to study well communication. Results show that the well line is required to be aligned with the direction of the maximum compressive stress in order to link two wellbores when no fracture exists before hydraulic fracturing. Well communication becomes easy when one or more fractures are pre-existing between the wellbores.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
